- "broad": General or exploratory topic queries ("what is diabetes", "chris pratt", "history of AI").
  - MAIN = foundational defining facts. AUX = statistics, supplementary details.
  - Document must provide substantial coverage of at least ONE main aspect to qualify for 3+.
- "specific": Queries requesting a specific or closed answer ("release date of X", "who won the game", "net worth of Y").
  - MAIN = the specific requested fact. Nothing else substitutes.
  - Hard gate: Missing the specific answer = capped at 2/SM, regardless of how much related context is provided. A document that authoritatively corrects the query's false premise counts as providing the answer.
- "list": Comparisons, multi-item requests, pros-and-cons ("X vs Y", "top 10 movies", "benefits and risks of Z").
  - MAIN = coverage of all requested items/aspects.
  - Hard gate: Covering <50% of requested items = capped at 2/SM.
